# Clinics — module-only migrations & seeders

## Requirement

**Never** add new clinic-domain migrations, seeders, or **notifications** under:

- `database/migrations/`
- `database/seeders/`
- `app/Notifications/` (clinic portal / appointment / booking types)

Clinic notifications belong in `Modules/Clinics/app/Infrastructure/Notifications/`.  
Orchestration helper: `Modules/Clinics/app/Application/Services/ClinicPortalNotifications.php`.

Clinic ERP tables (`clinics`, `clinic_*`, `clinical_*`, `episodes_of_care`, `waitlists`, `sessions`, `treatment_programs_*`, `booking_slots`, `doctor_*`, `equipment_inventory`, `assessment_templates`, `clinic_wallets`, `rcm_*`, …) belong in:

| What | Where |
|---|---|
| Migrations | `Modules/Clinics/database/migrations/` |
| Seeders | `Modules/Clinics/database/seeders/` |
| Sync tooling | `Modules/Clinics/app/Infrastructure/Migration/CollectSharedClinic*.php` |

## Sync from legacy (one-time / drift repair)

```bash
php artisan clinics:collect-migrations --force
php artisan clinics:collect-seeders --force
```

## Testing

```bash
php artisan migrate --path=Modules/Clinics/database/migrations --env=testing
./vendor/bin/pest Modules/Clinics/tests/
```

- **No** `migrate:fresh` on shared dev DB — see `no-migrate-fresh.mdc`
- `ClinicsServiceProvider` loads module migrations via `loadMigrationsFrom()`

## Cross-module exceptions

- `patients` table: shared with `Modules/Patients` — clinic migrations may reference it; Patients module owns PHI models
- Insurance billing tables: `Modules/Insurance`
- Ecommerce / Inventory / Jobs tables: their respective modules
